+        //
+        // Every entry is a WEAK reference, and that is the whole trick: a weak
+        // undefined symbol links to a null address instead of failing, and does
+        // not drag the archive member that would define it into the link. So
+        // the table costs only its own entries, and an entry for a type this
+        // binary never links resolves to null -- which is exactly the contract
+        // jsGetExportedSymbol has, so the bridge's existing fallback path stays
